.TH VAC-SUB 8 "2026-05-30" "vx-dga-l-vac" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
vac-sub \- VAC sub-instance daemon for multi-server registration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vac-sub
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vac-sub
runs the full VAC registration loop for a named sub-instance, enabling
a single machine to register simultaneously in multiple VAS servers.
.PP
It inherits the base configuration from
.I /etc/vac/vac.conf
and overrides it with
.IR /etc/vac/vac.sub/NAME/vac.conf .
State is kept independently in
.IR /var/lib/vac/sub/NAME/ .
.PP
The sub-instance UUID is derived deterministically using UUID v5
(SHA-1, namespace = main UUID, name = NAME), so the same machine and
name always produce the same UUID on the VAS server.
.PP
Log messages are prefixed with
.BI [ NAME-VAC ]
to allow filtering with
.IR journalctl .
.PP
.B vac-sub
is normally launched and supervised by
.BR vac-sub-manager (8).
It can also be run standalone via
.BR vac-sub.service (8).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/vac/vac.sub/NAME/vac.conf
Sub-instance configuration (overrides base config).
.TP
.I /etc/vac/vac.sub/NAME/.enabled
Presence of this file enables the sub-instance in
.BR vac-sub-manager (8).
.TP
.I /var/lib/vac/sub/NAME/
State directory: UUID, version, identity, extras.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vac (8),
.BR vac-sub-manager (8),
.BR vac-sub-instance (8)
